<!--
  1vivy personal crDroid 16.0 ROM - OnePlus SM8850 (infiniti, macan, macanc,
  fairlady). FEATURES-V6 BOOTSTRAP GOVERNED MANIFEST.

  Drop into .repo/local_manifests/ as 1vivy-features-v6.xml after:

      repo init -u https://github.com/crdroidandroid/android.git -b 16.0
      # base manifest pinned at a311bc97e4784ee24e8f97e377d06bdbff85b4bb

  then `repo sync`.

  USE THIS FILE INSTEAD OF 1vivy-rom.xml, 1vivy-features-v2.xml,
  1vivy-features-v4.xml AND 1vivy-features-v5.xml - NEVER ALONGSIDE ANY OF
  THEM. They declare overlapping paths, so placing two in local_manifests/
  at once is a configuration error.

  THIS MANIFEST IS PUBLISHED-HEAD COMPOSITION. DO NOT run
  patches/patch/apply-patches.py against a tree synced from this file: the
  camera-port profile already present in governed inherited heads would be
  DOUBLE-APPLIED. 1vivy-rom.xml is the opposite lane.

  WHY THIS BOOTSTRAP EXISTS. It binds exactly twenty independently confirmed
  carrier-only 1vivy repositories to staging/bootstrap/features-v6 before
  feature topic composition begins. It deliberately does not name
  staging/features-v6/all. The other fourteen infiniti-camera-port projects
  remain input-only sync sources.

  Derived from 1vivy-features-v5.xml by retaining all unaffected external and
  sync-source projects, moving the eleven inherited governed rows to the
  carrier branch, replacing frameworks/native and the QCOM audio project, and
  adding the other seven governed A23 projects. Only
  lineage_infiniti-bp4a-userdebug is intended for later runtime validation;
  no runtime result is implied here.
-->
